          "message": {
            "text": "Public ask page loses request-disconnect cancellation\n\nThe server page constructs a new header-only Request and runs provider-backed ask work with its fresh signal, so browser disconnects cannot cancel the underlying provider operation.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Resource exhaustion\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-400\n\nRemediation:\nMove page generation through the cancellation-aware API or another handler that owns the real request signal and abort provider work when its consumer disconnects."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:b3a421af354424968ec5f245cff341a108b65b58f14d3e9c83a2998231161cde"
